        <body>
            <div xml:id="d557">

                <pb facs="0561" n="1295" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1295"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr. Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-08-26"><hi rendition="#italic">August 26, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received, Sept. 7.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 603.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that the
                    murderer of Mr. Stupe, of whose first trial you were informed in my No. 537, of
                    May 5, 1895, has been sentenced on retrial to fifteen years’ imprisonment.</p>
                <p>The reversal of the first judgment by the court of cassation without the presence
                    of the consular dragoman caused my protest to the Porte, copy of which was sent
                    you in my dispatch No. 529, of May 3, 1895. The result of retrial was as
                    gratifying as it was unexpected.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. W. Terrell.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
